ardenbaai_Bay_Lagoon_L.G._Smith_Blvd._-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Francis of Assisi Church, Oranjestad","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.5224,"lo":-70.0349,"d":593,"ds":"The St. Francis of Assisi Church (Papiamento: Parokia San Francisco di Asis Dutch: Sint Franciscus Kerk) also alternatively called Pro Cathedral of St.","wpu":"St. Francis of Assisi Church, Oranjestad","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/Sta._Franciscuskerk.JPG/960px-Sta._Franciscuskerk.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Oranjestad Reef Islands","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.509444,"lo":-70.039167,"d":959,"ds":"The Oranjestad Reef Islands lie just off the western coast of the island of Aruba, a constituent island nation of the Kingdom of the Netherlands in the Dutch Caribbean, adjacent to the central harbour of the capital Oranjestad. They form a 309 ha site encompassing sand and boulder coral islets, on a substrate of submerged reef, which can vary in size and shape following winter storms and hurricanes.","wpu":"Oranjestad Reef Islands","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Luchtopname._Oranjestad%2C_Aruba.%2C_Bestanddeelnr_935-1225.jpg/960px-Luchtopname._Oranjestad%2C_Aruba.%2C_Bestanddeelnr_935-1225.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"National Library of Aruba","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.5151,"lo":-70.0295,"d":977,"ds":"The National Library of Aruba (Papiamento: Biblioteca Nacional Aruba, BNA) is the main library of Aruba. It is located in Oranjestad and holds more than 100,000 volumes. BNA serves as both the national and the public library of Aruba.","wpu":"National Library of Aruba","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/71/Logo_bna_new_2024.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Tanki Leendert","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.5416,"lo":-70.01989,"d":3278,"ds":"Tanki Leendert is a town in Noord on the island of Aruba. The parish of Tanki Leendert has been split from Noord since 1968.","wpu":"Tanki Leendert","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Catholic_church_Kapel_Monte_Calvario%2C_Tanki_Leendert.JPG/960px-Catholic_church_Kapel_Monte_Calvario%2C_Tanki_Leendert.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. Philomena's Church, Paradera","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.5356,"lo":-70.0043,"d":4148,"ds":"The St. Philomena's Church (Papiamento: Parokia Santa Filomena Dutch: St. Filomenakerk) is a religious building belonging to the Catholic Church located in the town of Paradera, on the Caribbean island of Aruba, an autonomous country in the Kingdom of the Netherlands in the Lesser Antilles.","wpu":"St. Philomena's Church, Paradera","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/ca/Filomenakerk%2C_Plaza_Louis_Eusabio_Kraanwinkel%2C_Paradera_3.JPG/960px-Filomenakerk%2C_Plaza_Louis_Eusabio_Kraanwinkel%2C_Paradera_3.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Hooiberg","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.517,"lo":-69.995,"d":4669,"ds":"Hooiberg (Dutch: /ˈɦojbɛrx/ ()) is a distinctively shaped, 165 m (541 ft) conical hill located at the heart of the island of Aruba. This geological formation is a prominent and recognizable landmark that has long captured the attention of locals and visitors alike—Hooiberg is Aruba's centerpiece.","wpu":"Hooiberg","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Aruba-Hooiberg-2013.JPG/960px-Aruba-Hooiberg-2013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Bubali Bird Sanctuary","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.559722,"lo":-70.049444,"d":4802,"ds":"The Bubali Bird Sanctuary (Dutch: Bubali vogelreservaat) form a 20 ha wetland area at the north-western end of the island of Aruba, a constituent country of the Dutch Caribbean.","wpu":"Bubali Bird Sanctuary","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Bubali_Bird_Sanctuary%2C_Palm_Beach%2C_Aruba%2C_Sep_2018.jpg/960px-Bubali_Bird_Sanctuary%2C_Palm_Beach%2C_Aruba%2C_Sep_2018.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St Ann's Church, Aruba","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.5625,"lo":-70.0313,"d":5001,"ds":"St Ann's Church is a Roman Catholic Church located along the northern portion of Aruba island within the Catholic Diocese of Willemstad. Although rebuilt several times, the church traces its history back to 1776. It temporarily closed for repairs due to damage in 2011 and has since reopened.","wpu":"St Ann's Church, Aruba","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b9/Aruba_-_St._Anna_Church.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Palm Beach, Aruba","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.568775,"lo":-70.042181,"d":5664,"ds":"Palm Beach is a tourism district about 6 kilometers (3.7 miles) northwest of Oranjestad, the capital of Aruba. Many high-rise hotels are located there, such as Hyatt Regency Aruba Resort & Casino, Aruba Marriott Resort & Stellaris Casino, Barceló, Holiday Inn SunSpree Resort, Ritz Carlton Resort, and RIU Palace Aruba.","wpu":"Palm Beach, Aruba","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Palm-Beach-Aruba-2013.JPG/960px-Palm-Beach-Aruba-2013.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Excelsior Casino","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.575393,"lo":-70.044197,"d":6417,"ds":"Excelsior Casino was a casino located in Aruba as part of the Holiday Inn hotel. It was the first casino to open on the island. It originally was known as the King Casino, then become the Grand Holiday Casino before adopting its final name in 2000.","wpu":"Excelsior Casino","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Xanadu_Casino.jpg/960px-Xanadu_Casino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Aruba","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.515,"lo":-69.975,"d":6846,"ds":"Aruba, officially the Country of Aruba, is an island constituent country within the Kingdom of the Netherlands, in the southern Caribbean Sea 29 kilometres (18 mi) north of the Venezuelan peninsula of Paraguaná and 80 kilometres (50 mi) north-west of Curaçao. In 1986, Aruba became a constituent country within the Kingdom of the Netherlands and acquired the official name.","wpu":"Aruba","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Flag_of_Aruba.svg/960px-Flag_of_Aruba.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Aruba Marriott Resort & Stellaris Casino","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.580821,"lo":-70.042987,"d":7006,"ds":"The Aruba Marriott Resort & Stellaris Casino is a hotel and casino complex located along Palm Beach on the northwestern coast of Aruba. The Atrium-style Resort is situated on 10 oceanfront acres with 600 feet of beach frontage. The property opened in 1995, and is part of the Marriott Hotels & Resorts portfolio.","wpu":"Aruba Marriott Resort & Stellaris Casino","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/58/Aruba_Marriott_Resort_%26_Stellaris_Casino.jpg/960px-Aruba_Marriott_Resort_%26_Stellaris_Casino.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Alto Vista Chapel","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.5759,"lo":-70.0109,"d":7078,"ds":"Alto Vista Chapel is a small Catholic chapel that stands on the hills above the north shore of the sea and to the northeast of the town of Noord, on the island of Aruba, 27 km north of the coast of Venezuela. The church, painted on the outside in stark bright yellow, makes it a conspicuous religious monument for people to visit.","wpu":"Alto Vista Chapel","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/80/Chapel_at_Alto_Vista_front_and_right_side.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Palm Island, Aruba","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.469722,"lo":-69.984722,"d":7891,"ds":"Palm Island is a small private island near Aruba, Kingdom of the Netherlands, serving as a tourist attraction. The island is a 5-minute ferry ride from the mainland. The island includes a small beach and a water park.","wpu":"Palm Island, Aruba","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2f/Balashi_De_Palm_Island_Ferry_Terminal_-_panoramio.jpg/960px-Balashi_De_Palm_Island_Ferry_Terminal_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Frenchman's Pass","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.485833,"lo":-69.972222,"d":7986,"ds":"Franse Pas (in Dutch) or Rooi Frances (in Papiamento) (literally: Frenchman's Pass) is a narrow passage on the island of Aruba, nestled between coral cliffs in Balashi. Frenchman's pass is located north of the area known as Spanish Lagoon and near the remnants of the Balashi Gold Mine.","wpu":"Frenchman's Pass","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/90/Frenchmans_Pass%2C_Aruba_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Santa Cruz, Aruba","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.5,"lo":-69.966667,"d":7998,"ds":"Santa Cruz (Dutch pronunciation: [saːntaː.kruːz]) is a Region and Town in central Aruba, dominated by the Arikok National Park. The town is connected by Highway 7 from west to east and Highway 4 from north to south. The district has an area of 41.04 square kilometers and 12,870 inhabitants according to the 2010 census.","wpu":"Santa Cruz, Aruba","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f1/ARIKOK_NATIONAL_PARK_-_DAIMARI_BAY_-_panoramio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Spaans Lagoen","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.47685,"lo":-69.97258,"d":8448,"ds":"Spaans Lagoen, which translates to \"Spanish lagoon\", is a coastal bay and wetland area of Aruba. Designated as a Ramsar site since 1980, and in February 2017, it was included within the boundary of the Arikok National Park. It is the only inner bay of Aruba and was formed during the last ice age.","wpu":"Spaans Lagoen","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/bd/Balashi_goudsmelterij_looking_over_Spaans_Lagoen_area.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Aruba Natural Bridge","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.541111,"lo":-69.958333,"d":9021,"ds":"The Aruba Natural Bridge was a tourist attraction in Aruba that was formed naturally out of coral limestone. It collapsed on 2 September 2005. The natural arch, measuring approximately 25 feet (7.6 m) high and 100 feet (30 m) long, was the remnant of an ancient cave.","wpu":"Aruba Natural Bridge","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0b/197306_aruba_naturalbridge.jpg/960px-197306_aruba_naturalbridge.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Pos Chiquito","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":12.46508,"lo":-69.96842,"d":9575,"ds":"Pos Chiquito or Pos Chikito is a town in Savaneta on the island of Aruba. It is located on the main road between Oranjestad and San Nicolaas. It has become known for its coral reef, and has a small diving cove.","wpu":"Pos Chiquito","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/AH..._WHO_LOOKING_SO_SWEET.jpg/960px-AH..._WHO_LOOKING_SO_SWEET.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Oranjestad (UK: orr-AN-yə-staht, US: or-AHN-, oh-RAHN-, Dutch: [oːˈrɑɲəstɑt]; literally \"Orange City\" in Dutch; Papiamento: Playa, lit. 'beach'), the capital and most populous of Aruba's eight regions, is located on the southwestern coast of the island. Administratively, the Oranjestad is divided into two regions: East and West. In 2010, the capital had a population of 28,294, and by 2020, it increased to 28,658.","wpu":"Oranjestad","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f8/Sightings_in_Oranjestad.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}